# What does NOT go into the .vsix.
#
# Inverted from .gitignore's logic: everything is included unless listed, so
# this file is the one place a stray artifact gets caught. vsce already
# drops devDependencies (@vscode/vsce, ovsx and their ~330 packages) by
# asking `npm ls --omit=dev`, so none of them need a rule here; what needs
# one is everything else that can sit in this folder.
#
# After changing this file, look at what actually ships:
#
#   npx vsce ls
#
# The intended shape is the extension's own src/ and media/, the manifest,
# README, CHANGELOG and LICENSE, and node_modules/hoverlab as real files.

# Editor and tooling state.
.vscode/**
.vscode-test/**
.github/**
**/.eslintrc.json
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# Build products of this very folder. A .vsix packaged earlier must never be
# folded into the next one, and a `npm pack` tarball of the CLI is a
# leftover of the old file: recipe.
*.vsix
**/*.vsix
*.tgz
**/*.tgz

# Anything that could hold a credential. Nothing here reads one from disk
# (the licence key lives in ~/.hoverlab, outside the project), so a match
# is always a mistake.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# Source maps and dev-only files.
**/*.map
**/*.test.js
**/*.test.mjs
**/test/**
**/tests/**
package-lock.json

# The one runtime dependency IS shipped, since the extension does nothing
# without it, but its own development files and its README are not. The npm
# tarball only carries bin/, src/ and README.md, so this is belt and braces
# for the day someone links a checkout again.
node_modules/hoverlab/node_modules/**
node_modules/hoverlab/README.md
node_modules/.package-lock.json
node_modules/.bin/**
